WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.644 --> 00:00:16.745
stared at the huge door.

2
00:00:16.765 --> 00:00:20.589
"Did you ring the doorbell to see if anyone's home?"

3
00:00:21.249 --> 00:00:22.370
Detective Smith groaned.

4
00:00:24.952 --> 00:00:25.713
Roxy chuckled.

5
00:00:26.914 --> 00:00:28.576
"I made the same joke."

6
00:00:30.409 --> 00:00:32.070
Cozlin laughed and then pushed on the door.

7
00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:37.934
"Grr!" "That won't work," Roxy said.

8
00:00:37.954 --> 00:00:40.015
"Even I can't open it."

9
00:00:43.398 --> 00:00:44.258
Cozlin shrugged.

10
00:00:44.278 --> 00:00:45.919
"It was worth a try.

11
00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.021
Let's see if I can move through it."

12
00:00:49.902 --> 00:00:52.084
She took a deep breath and stepped into the door.

13
00:00:53.925 --> 00:00:56.027
Zimp! She was on the other side!

14
00:00:56.627 --> 00:00:57.728
The air felt chilly.

15
00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:00.101
"Hey, Rocket Girl!"

16
00:01:00.482 --> 00:01:01.042
she shouted.

17
00:01:01.543 --> 00:01:02.964
Her watch beeped, and she opened it.

18
00:01:02.984 --> 00:01:06.927
"Be quiet!"

19
00:01:07.368 --> 00:01:08.108
Roxy whispered.

20
00:01:08.128 --> 00:01:11.511
"Something's in there, and we don't want to wake it up again!"

21
00:01:11.531 --> 00:01:14.054
"Oops," Cozlin whispered.

22
00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:22.001
"Sorry!" She flew down the long, dark tunnel, which opened into a large chamber.

23
00:01:24.103 --> 00:01:25.264
The air felt warmer.

24
00:01:25.964 --> 00:01:29.306
Torches lit the chamber, and piles of shiny gold lay everywhere.

25
00:01:30.707 --> 00:01:31.667
Cozlin gasped.

26
00:01:31.687 --> 00:01:35.470
"I never saw so much—" Snort!

27
00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:38.671
Cozlin dropped flat to the ground.

28
00:01:39.212 --> 00:01:40.052
She wasn't alone.

29
00:01:40.592 --> 00:01:41.833
She peered through the darkness.

30
00:01:42.614 --> 00:01:44.275
Something was on the other side of the chamber.

31
00:01:45.175 --> 00:01:46.856
She grabbed a torch and moved closer.

32
00:01:51.739 --> 00:01:53.460
In the torchlight Cozlin saw a tail.

33
00:01:54.292 --> 00:01:57.313
Her eyes followed the tail to a large, scaly body.

34
00:01:57.893 --> 00:02:01.714
Wings lay folded along its back, and sharp claws grew from its feet.

35
00:02:01.734 --> 00:02:04.835
"It's a dragon!"

36
00:02:05.275 --> 00:02:05.975
Cozlin thought.

37
00:02:06.755 --> 00:02:08.036
The dragon snorted again.

38
00:02:08.556 --> 00:02:09.756
It turned its head toward her.

39
00:02:11.117 --> 00:02:12.137
Cozlin held her breath.

40
00:02:12.817 --> 00:02:14.378
Then she let out a sigh of relief.

41
00:02:16.598 --> 00:02:19.259
The beast's eyes were closed—it was asleep!

42
00:02:19.899 --> 00:02:23.020
She felt a blast of hot air as the dragon snored peacefully.

43
00:02:23.904 --> 00:02:26.025
"Why is this dragon down here?"

44
00:02:26.545 --> 00:02:27.025
she thought.

45
00:02:27.045 --> 00:02:30.006
"And why is all this gold down here?"

46
00:02:31.046 --> 00:02:34.267
Suddenly the dragon's tail twitched and sent gold coins flying.

47
00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:37.868
Cozlin panicked and flew as fast as she could.

48
00:02:40.649 --> 00:02:42.809
Zimp! She popped back through the door.

49
00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.930
"Well?" Roxy said.

50
00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:46.210
"What's down there?"

51
00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:48.231
Detective Smith took out his notepad.

52
00:02:48.251 --> 00:02:50.491
"Lots of gold!"

53
00:02:50.951 --> 00:02:51.632
Cozlin said.

54
00:02:51.652 --> 00:02:53.869
"Huh," Roxy said.

55
00:02:53.889 --> 00:02:57.111
"But what about the sound the construction workers heard?"

56
00:02:57.131 --> 00:02:58.472
"Oh, yeah."

57
00:02:58.952 --> 00:03:00.553
Cozlin scratched the back of her neck.

58
00:03:00.994 --> 00:03:03.075
"That was probably the dragon."

59
00:03:03.936 --> 00:03:05.517
Detective Smith dropped his notepad.

60
00:03:06.097 --> 00:03:06.818
"The what?"

61
00:03:06.838 --> 00:03:09.860
"But don't worry," Cozlin said quickly.

62
00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:11.441
"It's fast asleep.

63
00:03:11.942 --> 00:03:13.803
It won't even know we're taking the gold."

64
00:03:15.044 --> 00:03:17.225
"Whoa! Hold on," Roxy said.

65
00:03:17.245 --> 00:03:20.668
"That sounds dangerous—and it's stealing."

66
00:03:21.388 --> 00:03:25.752
"That gold obviously doesn't belong to anyone," Cozlin said.

67
00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:28.695
"And gold is really valuable on Delkor.

68
00:03:29.215 --> 00:03:30.556
We could do good things with it."

69
00:03:31.257 --> 00:03:32.318
Detective Smith nodded.

70
00:03:32.338 --> 00:03:34.600
"Nobody is going to claim that gold.

71
00:03:35.661 --> 00:03:38.864
And the police department needs new cars—and printers.

72
00:03:39.364 --> 00:03:41.125
Mine keeps getting jammed."

73
00:03:41.846 --> 00:03:42.647
Roxy frowned.

74
00:03:42.667 --> 00:03:44.649
"I'm surprised at you two.

75
00:03:45.149 --> 00:03:48.212
We're not touching that gold till we find out more about it.

76
00:03:48.744 --> 00:03:51.667
And right now that dragon isn't bothering anyone.

77
00:03:52.547 --> 00:03:53.708
Let's keep it that way!"

78
00:03:57.051 --> 00:03:58.533
Cozlin was back on Delkor.

79
00:03:59.994 --> 00:04:02.896
She was in the palace, telling King Radnik about her discovery.

80
00:04:03.717 --> 00:04:04.658
His face lit up.

81
00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:07.480
"That's amazing, Kid Comet.

82
00:04:08.001 --> 00:04:11.163
We could build new schools and hospitals with that gold!"

83
00:04:12.304 --> 00:04:14.006
"I know," she said.

84
00:04:14.806 --> 00:04:16.228
The king paced back and forth.

85
00:04:17.048 --> 00:04:19.870
"And you're sure the Earthlings don't want it?"

86
00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:23.352
"Uh, yeah," Cozlin said.

87
00:04:23.372 --> 00:04:25.914
"I guess gold isn't valuable there."

88
00:04:26.695 --> 00:04:28.096
The king stopped pacing.

89
00:04:28.156 --> 00:04:31.258
"Well, gold is very valuable here.

90
00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:34.500
I'll have a portal prepared immediately."
